I really like pets as a wizard.  I scour the mines for a magic whistle,
and I'm just patient if I don't find one...  I'll have 2-3 dogs/cats. 
(And I'll look for polymorph traps - *I* have MR, so I can walk into them :-) )

I'm a big fan of "go down in a dungeon level until you meet something
nasty...then run away!"

And I'm sure opinions differ on this one, but Wizards can still Melee (or
throw daggers).  I try to save Pw for those times I really need it (e.g.,
3 rothes in a line...one if I'm full on Pw and feeling cocky.  If there
are three out there, but only one near my...my favorite is to get into a
corridor and stick a pet between me and them.  Wait until they bunch up,
and *then* let'm have it with a force bolt!)  But anything smaller then an
ant or a rothe?  Hack 'em to bits!  (Ok, orcs can be dangerous, too...) 
Be sure to always take them on in corridors if you do have to fight them
hand to hand...

Armor for a wizard:
*Somewhere* you'll find either Leather or Studded Leather - wear it.
Find a helmit.  Keep trying on helmits until you get an enchanted one. 
All else fails, wear a dwarven helm - it screws up your armor as much as
an orcish helm, but has +2 armor.  Wear Iron shoes, if all else fails. 
Remember that High boots are also +2 and, when combines with a metal helm,
gives usually ~3% spell failure - I find that acceptable.  Let a pet kill
the MineTown watch (if it can!) and see if you get gloves.  Those little
points of armor add up, and at least they protect you from orcs...

Down on hitpoints?  Well..nothing says you can't run back to level 3, wait
'till you heal, and come back.  I'll get into situations where I"ll go
down the stairs, kill one orc, and run back upstairs to heal...if anything
shows up, I'll run up *another* level.  When I'm strong, I'll re-clear the
1st, and then go kill a 2nd orc...  Cowardly, but it works :-)

